.TH AVR\-SERVICE\-TOKEN\-VIEW 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-service-token-view \- Show a service token's details, versions and grants.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr service-token view
[OPTIONS] TOKEN_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show a service token's details, versions and grants.
.PP
Reads a revoked or expired token as well. Its grants are removed when it is revoked and 30 days after it expires. The secret itself is never shown again after `avr service-token create` or `rotate`.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr service-token view <token-id>
    avr service-token view <token-id> --json grants
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    blocked_by, created_at, created_by, expires_at, expiring_soon, grants,
    grants_version, group_id, id, last_used_at, name, organization_id,
    previous_valid_until, revoked_at, revoked_reason, rotated_at,
    rotation_version, status
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fITOKEN_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-service-token (1),
.BR avr-service-token-create (1),
.BR avr-service-token-list (1),
.BR avr-service-token-revoke (1),
.BR avr-service-token-revoke-all (1),
.BR avr-service-token-rotate (1),
.BR avr-service-token-set-access (1)
